<title>UK: UK's Henlys chairman Doherty to stand down.</title>
<headline>UK's Henlys chairman Doherty to stand down.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>British motor vehicle distributor Henlys Plc said on Friday its chairman, Michael Doherty, would stand down after the company's annual meeting in April.</p>
<p>Henlys said Doherty would be succeeded by Norman Askew, who joined as a non-executive director last year.  </p>
<p>&quot;This has been a very successful year for the group, and we remain encouraged by the outlook for 1997,&quot; Doherty said in a statement.</p>
<p>Henlys' pretax profits rose 32 percent in 1996 to 33.3 million stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
